WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:04.238
Exercise 4 asks for billing rows that are not
definitely Paid including

00:00:04.264 --> 00:00:09.351
records where the payment status is missing That
final phrase is the

00:00:09.364 --> 00:00:13.824
important part If you use ordinary not equal to Paid
rows with

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:18.257
null status will disappear because the result is
UNKNOWN So you need

00:00:18.283 --> 00:00:23.798
the null-safe comparison we practiced earlier
Complete the WHERE clause

00:00:23.824 --> 00:00:28.558
in the browser then select Run and Check You can
also copy

00:00:28.584 --> 00:00:32.991
the query into pgAdmin and compare ordinary
inequality with the null-safe version

00:00:33.907 --> 00:00:38.753
This is a short exercise but it tests an important
idea Before

00:00:38.778 --> 00:00:43.327
writing the operator translate the requirement into
plain language include anything that

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:46.420
is different from Paid even if the current status is
missing
